<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ugyen Wangchuck</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1862">1862</a>–<a href="/years/1926">1926</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ugyen Wangchuck was the first hereditary king of Bhutan, elected by an assembly of clergy, officials and leading families at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punakha">Punakha</a> in 1907. As penlop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trongsa">Trongsa</a> he defeated his rivals in the civil wars of the late 19th century and won British favour by helping the Younghusband expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> in 1904. The 1910 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-punakha">Treaty of Punakha</a> placed Bhutan's foreign relations under British guidance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ugyen-wangchuck.jpg" alt="Ugyen Wangchuck" width="320" height="373" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Claude White · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ugyen_Wangchuck,_1905_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the 1870s rivalry between the valleys of Paro and Tongsa brought civil war, from which <b>Ugyen Wangchuck</b>, penlop of Trongsa, emerged to unite the country in 1882–85.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-bhutan">Kingdom of Bhutan · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Ugyen Wangchuck</b>, penlop of Trongsa, emerged supreme, and in 1907 an assembly elected him hereditary king, creating the Kingdom of Bhutan.</blockquote><a href="/state/zhabdrung-bhutan">Zhabdrung Bhutan</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Bumthang District, in what is now <a href="/countries/bhutan">Bhutan</a>. Died in Bumthang District, in what is now <a href="/countries/bhutan">Bhutan</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=27.75,90.67&amp;year=1903" aria-label="Bumthang District on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6929 1147 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ugyen Wangchuck"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7379 1417h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7379 1417h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=27.75,90.67&amp;year=1903">What was here in 1903? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
